                <pb facs="0439" n="427" sameAs="frus:frus1942v01/pg427"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">390.1115A/860: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-06-09T14:00:00-04:00">June 9, 1942—2 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1485. American interests—Japan. Your 2543, June 6, 8 p.m., final paragraph. Your
                    action approved, as officials and nationals of Canada and other American
                    Republics must obviously be given full equality in all respects with United
                    States officials and nationals and the Department desires that all persons
                    traveling on the vessel be given accommodations suitable to their relative rank
                    and position regardless of nationality.</p>
                <p>Swiss Legation Tokyo should be informed that Department accordingly supports its
                    position.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
